<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Rex Trueform yr shr falls, flat 1997 seen.</title>
<headline>Rex Trueform yr shr falls, flat 1997 seen.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended Dec 31</p>
<p>		 (million of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)	  21.3	vs 26.8</p>
<p>    Attrib income     3.9	vs  4.5</p>
<p>    Tax		   1.1	vs  2.5</p>
<p>    Interest received 1.8	vs  1.1</p>
<p>    Turnover	  105.3	vs 108.8</p>
<p>Full name: Rex Trueform Clothing Company Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE:  The group said it continued to face difficult trading conditions and had lost large orders for parastatal corporate clothing. Exports were regarded as a priority but government support was needed. Profits in the current year were unlikely to exeed those of 1996 but it was well positoned to benefit from continued growth in its Queenspark division.</p>
<p>The group declared a cumulative preference dividend totalling 8,400 rand.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
